<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: Review a pull request" id="Pull-Request-Details">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Open: double-click a pull request in the <control>AZD Pull Requests</control> tool window</p>
        <p>Mark a file as viewed: <shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+S</shortcut> (macOS: see <ui-path>Settings | Keymap</ui-path>)</p>
        <p>Timeline: <control>View Timeline</control> in the pull request details</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Open a pull request, check out its branch, go through the changed files and the timeline and read its status and branch policies.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Inspect an Azure DevOps pull request: files, diffs, timeline, checks and branch policies.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Review Azure DevOps pull requests in JetBrains IDEs with AZD: changed files, diffs, viewed state,
        timeline, branch policies, build checks and linked work items.</web-summary>

    <p>
        When you open a pull request, AZD shows its details in a tab of the <control>AZD Pull Requests</control> tool window.
        The tab title is the pull request number, for example <control>!42</control>.
        From the details, you open diffs and the timeline, check out the branch and see what blocks the merge.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Open a pull request" id="azd_view_and_apply_changes">
        <procedure title="Open a pull request and read its details" id="azd-view-apply-procedure">
            <step>
                Open the <control>AZD Pull Requests</control> tool window.
                For the ways to open it, see <a href="Work-with-Azure-DevOps-pull-requests.topic" anchor="open-tool-window"/>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Double-click a pull request in the list.
            </step>
            <step>
                Read the header of the details tab:
                <list>
                    <li>The title and the pull request number. Click the number to open the pull request in the browser.</li>
                    <li><control>View Timeline</control> opens the discussion and history; see <a anchor="azd_pull_request_timeline"/>.</li>
                    <li>The commit selector shows the changes from all commits. Select one commit to see only its changes.</li>
                    <li>The source branch. Click it to check it out; see <a anchor="check-out-branch"/>.</li>
                </list>
                <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_details.png" alt="Pull request details tab with changed files, review status and the action buttons" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Double-click a file in the changed files tree to open its diff.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            Right-click the pull request title for <control>Refresh Pull Request</control>, <control>Review with AI</control>,
            <control>Open Pull Request in Browser</control> and <control>Copy Pull Request URL</control>.
            The right-click menu of the changed files tree also has <control>Link Work Item</control>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Check out the pull request branch" id="check-out-branch">
        <secondary-label ref="azd_version"/>
        <p>
            Click the source branch name in the details header to open the branch popup:
        </p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Checkout">
                Fetches the source branch and checks it out in the current working tree.
            </def>
            <def title="Open in Worktree">
                Fetches the source branch and opens it in a new Git worktree, so your current branch stays untouched.
                The option appears for active pull requests that are not from a fork, when the branch is not checked out yet
                and the project has a single Git repository.
            </def>
            <def title="Show in Git Log">
                Shows the source branch in the <control>Git</control> tool window.
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_branch_popup.png" alt="Branch popup of a pull request with Checkout, Open in Worktree and Show in Git Log" -->
        <p>
            Some features need the branch locally, for example <a href="Azd-PR-Comments.topic" anchor="suggested-changes">applying suggested changes</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Review on the current branch" id="review-mode">
        <p>
            When the checked-out branch has an open pull request, the branch popup of the main toolbar shows
            <control>Pull request !N on</control> followed by the branch name, with these actions:
        </p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Show Pull Request in the Tool window">
                Opens the details of the pull request.
            </def>
            <def title="Review Mode">
                Shows the review comments of the pull request in the regular editor.
            </def>
            <def title="Update to Enable Review Mode…">
                Appears when your local branch is out of sync with the remote branch.
                Updates the branch so that comments match the code.
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_review_mode.png" alt="Git branch popup showing the pull request of the current branch and the Review Mode option" -->
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Go through the changed files" id="changed-files">
        <p>
            The changed files tree shows how many comments each file has and whether you have viewed it.
            The progress line, for example <control>Viewed: 3 out of 7</control>, tracks your review.
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>To mark a file as viewed, right-click it and select <control>Mark as Viewed</control>, or press <shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+S</shortcut>. Press it again for <control>Mark as Not Viewed</control>.</li>
            <li>To show only some files, use the filter above the tree: <control>All Files</control>, <control>Unviewed Only</control> or <control>Viewed Only</control>.</li>
            <li>To mark every file you open as viewed, select <control>Automatically mark opened files as viewed</control> in <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | Preferences</ui-path>.</li>
        </list>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_files_filter.png" alt="Changed files tree with the Unviewed Only filter selected and one file marked as viewed" -->
        <note>
            <p>
                AZD saves the viewed state to Azure DevOps, so it follows you to the browser and other machines.
                This needs the <control>Full access</control> option when you sign in with Microsoft, or a full-access personal access token (PAT).
                With standard access, the viewed state is not available.
                To change the access level, sign in again; see <a href="Azd-Installation.topic" anchor="connect"/>.
            </p>
        </note>
        <p>
            The right-click menu of a file also has <control>Show Diff</control>, <control>Show Diff in a New Tab</control>,
            <control>Jump to Source</control>, <control>View Options</control> for grouping, <control>Expand All</control> and <control>Collapse All</control>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Read the diff" id="diff-viewer">
        <p>
            The diff opens in an editor tab named <control>Diff for Pull Request !N</control>.
            Review comments appear between the lines, and the toolbar after <control>Review:</control> has these buttons:
        </p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Previous Comment, Next Comment">
                Move between the comments of the file.
                They use the <control>Previous Occurrence</control> and <control>Next Occurrence</control> shortcuts of your keymap,
                <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+Up</shortcut> and <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+Down</shortcut> on Windows and Linux.
                To see the macOS keys, search for these actions in <ui-path>Settings | Keymap</ui-path>.
            </def>
            <def title="Refresh Review Data">
                Reloads the comments of the pull request.
            </def>
            <def title="AI button">
                Creates AI draft comments for the file; see <a href="AI-Pull-Request-Review.topic" anchor="ai_draft_comments"/>.
            </def>
            <def title="Submit Comments">
                Publishes your draft comments; see <a href="Azd-PR-Comments.topic" anchor="draft-comments"/>.
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            To hide or show comments in the diff, right-click the gutter of the diff, point to <control>Show Review Discussions</control> and select which comments to show.
            To add comments, see <a href="Azd-PR-Comments.topic"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Read the timeline" id="azd_pull_request_timeline">
        <p>
            The timeline shows the description and the history of the pull request in one editor tab.
        </p>
        <procedure title="Open and filter the timeline" id="azd-timeline-procedure">
            <step>
                In the pull request details, click <control>View Timeline</control>.
                <p>
                    The <control>Timeline for !N</control> tab opens.
                    It starts with the author, the source and target branches and the description, followed by the events.
                </p>
                <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_timeline.png" alt="Pull request timeline with the description, a commits event, a comment thread and a vote" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Optional: to show only some events, click the filter icon in the timeline header and select event types.
                <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_timeline_filter.png" alt="Timeline event filter with Comments and Commits selected" -->
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="All Events">Every event.</def>
            <def title="Comments">Comment threads on the pull request and on files.</def>
            <def title="Commits">Pushes that added commits.</def>
            <def title="Votes">Reviewer votes.</def>
            <def title="State">State changes, such as completed, abandoned or reactivated.</def>
            <def title="Reviewers">Reviewers added or removed, and required or optional changes.</def>
            <def title="System">Other events created by Azure DevOps, such as policy messages.</def>
            <def title="My Comments/Replies">Threads that you started or replied to.</def>
            <def title="Active Comments">Threads that are still active.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            Click a commit in a commits event to open the pull request details with that commit selected.
            To open such links in the browser instead, clear <control>Open commit links from the timeline in the IDE</control> in <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | Preferences</ui-path>.
        </p>
        <p>
            The timeline lists events from oldest to newest.
            To show the newest events first, clear <control>Show events in the order ascending by date</control> in <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | UI Customization</ui-path>.
            To comment on the whole pull request from the timeline, see <a href="Azd-PR-Comments.topic" anchor="pr-level-comment"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Check the status and branch policies" id="azd_pull_request_status">
        <p>
            The bottom of the details tab lists what Azure DevOps requires before the pull request can be completed.
            Each row comes from a branch policy or a check on the target branch.
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_status_policies.png" alt="Status area of a pull request with work items, build checks, unresolved comments and reviewer rows" -->
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Work items: N, Details">
                The linked work items.
                Click <control>Details</control> to list them.
            </def>
            <def title="Work items must be linked">
                A policy requires at least one linked work item; see <a anchor="link-work-items"/>.
            </def>
            <def title="Comments must be resolved">
                A policy requires all comment threads to be resolved.
                Click <control>View Comments</control> to open the timeline with the comments.
            </def>
            <def title="Proof of presence is required">
                A policy requires an extra confirmation that you complete in Azure DevOps.
            </def>
            <def title="All required checks have passed, Checks in progress…, Checks failed">
                The summary of build validation policies.
                Click <control>Details…</control> to open the <control>Open in Pipeline View</control> popup and open a run.
                If a build has expired, AZD asks whether to re-trigger it.
            </def>
            <def title="Status Checks">
                Status policies that external services post to the pull request.
                Click <control>Details…</control> to see each check.
            </def>
            <def title="At least N reviewer(s) must approve">
                The minimum number of reviewers policy, including variants that do not count the author or the most recent pusher.
            </def>
            <def title="Required reviewers must approve">
                A required reviewer has not approved yet.
            </def>
            <def title="Reviewer rows">
                The vote of each reviewer; see <a href="Azd-PR-Complete.topic" anchor="reviewer-status"/>.
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            If <control>Open AZD links in tool window</control> is selected in <ui-path>Settings | Version Control | AZD | Preferences</ui-path>,
            build runs open in the <control>AZD Pipelines</control> tool window; otherwise, they open in the browser.
        </p>

        <chapter title="Merge status" id="merge-status">
            <secondary-label ref="azd_version"/>
            <p>
                Under the conflicts row, AZD explains merge outcomes that Azure DevOps reports:
            </p>
            <list>
                <li>A merge that Azure DevOps is still evaluating is shown as pending until the evaluation finishes.</li>
                <li><control>Azure DevOps rejected the merge because of a branch policy</control> appears when a policy blocks the merge.</li>
                <li><control>Azure DevOps could not compute the merge</control> appears when the merge cannot be calculated.</li>
            </list>
            <p>
                If the branches conflict, the conflicts row offers to resolve the conflicts locally.
            </p>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Link work items" id="link-work-items">
        <procedure title="Link a work item to a pull request" id="link-work-item-procedure">
            <step>
                Right-click the changed files tree of the pull request, or the timeline, and select <control>Link Work Item</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                In the <control>Link Work Item to Pull Request</control> dialog, select the <control>Project</control> and the <control>Work Item</control>.
                Clear <control>Only my work items</control> to search all work items.
                <!-- planned-image src="azd_pr_link_work_item_dialog.png" alt="Link Work Item to Pull Request dialog with a project and a work item selected" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Click <control>Link Work Item</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            AZD confirms with a <control>Work item linked</control> notification, or shows <control>Couldn't link work item</control> with the reason.
            To work with work items, see <a href="Azd-Boards.topic"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Comment, vote and complete" id="azd_review-actions">
        <list>
            <li>To comment on code, reply to threads and suggest changes, see <a href="Azd-PR-Comments.topic"/>.</li>
            <li>To vote, manage reviewers and complete or abandon the pull request, see <a href="Azd-PR-Complete.topic"/>.</li>
            <li>To let AI review the pull request, see <a href="AI-Pull-Request-Review.topic"/>.</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <seealso>
        <category ref="related">
            <a href="Work-with-Azure-DevOps-pull-requests.topic"/>
        </category>
        <category ref="external">
            <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/repos/git/review-pull-requests">Review pull requests (Microsoft Learn)</a>
            <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/repos/git/branch-policies">Branch policies (Microsoft Learn)</a>
        </category>
    </seealso>
</topic>
